Streams : 
==============
The stream module in Node.js is used to handle large data by reading it in small chunks instead of loading everything into memory.
If we import data from an Excel file without streams, the entire file is loaded into memory and then inserted into the database, which can cause memory issues.
When we use streams, the Excel file is read gradually. In our case, ExcelJS gives us one row at a time. We collect these rows into an array, and when the array reaches
 a fixed size like 100 records, we insert them into the database. This improves memory usage and performance.


